/*  Series — `a series of … with (…)`, `range … to …`, `For each`, `item … of`, `the number of`,
    `Insert`, `Remove` and setting an item — over numbers, text and facts.

    ★ A series is SHARED, as in the language: `Define t as s` names the same series, so an insert
      through `t` is seen through `s`. In C it is a pointer to one growable array.

    ★ One C type per kind of element — `cser_number`, `cser_text`, `cser_fact` — written into every
      program, used or not; C says nothing about a helper nobody calls. A series of anything else
      waits for a later slice.
*/

Pull books on collections, and the c-language.
    /// The kind of a series' elements, or "" when `kind` is no series.
    Bind text to element-of, given (the text kind):
        If kind starts with "series of ", return the characters from 11 to the end of kind.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// Whether a kind is one of the three a value can be on its own.
    Bind fact to is-scalar, given (the text kind):
        Return kind is "number" or kind is "text" or kind is "fact".
    Done.

    /// Whether a series can hold a kind: one of the three, an object, or a series that could itself.
    Bind fact to is-element-kind, given (the text kind):
        If cast element-of on (kind) is not "", return cast is-element-kind on (cast element-of on (kind)).
        If cast is-voidable on (kind), return cast is-element-kind on (cast voidable-inner on (kind)).
        Return cast is-scalar on (kind) or kind is "bits" or cast object-of on (kind) is not "" or cast is-union on (kind) or cast is-record on (kind)
            or cast is-map on (kind) or cast is-function on (kind).
    Done.

    /// Notes a series whose element is itself generated — a series, or a voidable — so its type is
    /// written with the generated ones, after what it holds. Kept as `held:<element>`, which no
    /// union or voidable entry can be mistaken for.
    Bind void to register-series unto emitter, given (the text element):
        Define entry as "held:{element}".
        If (the entry for entry in one's unions) is void:
            In one's unions, the entry for entry becomes true.
            Insert entry into one's union-order.
        Done.
    Done.

    /// The element a `held:` entry names, or "" for any other entry.
    Bind text to held-element, given (the text entry):
        If entry starts with "held:", return the characters from 6 to the end of entry.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// The C name of the series type that holds a kind.
    Bind text to series-c-name, given (the text element):
        // A series of series is named for what it holds: `cser_cser_text`.
        If cast element-of on (element) is not "", return "cser_{cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (element))}".
        If cast is-voidable on (element), return "cser_{cast voidable-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-union on (element), return "cser_{cast union-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-record on (element), return "cser_{cast record-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-map on (element), return "cser_{cast map-c-name on (element)}".
        // A series of axioms is its own type, so it prints them as `<axiom>`.
        If element starts with "axiom ", return "cser_ax_{cast function-c-name on (element)}".
        If cast is-function on (element), return "cser_{cast function-c-name on (element)}".
        Define object-name as cast object-of on (element).
        If object-name is not "", return "cser_obj_{cast c-ident on (object-name)}".
        Return "cser_{element}".
    Done.

    /// The C a series type and its helpers are, for elements of one kind.
    Bind text to c-series-helpers, given (the text element):
        Define held as cast c-type on (element).
        Define series-type as "{cast series-c-name on (element)}".
        Define written as cast write-call on (element, [s->data[i]]).
        Define equal as cast c-equal on (element, [s->data[i]], [v]).
        Define out as a chase.
        Insert "typedef struct {series-type}_s {series-type};\n" into out.
        Define c-language struct-series-type-form, given (the term series-type-s, the c-language axiom held),
            as [struct the series-type-s { the held* data; int len; int cap; CufetArena* home; };].
        Insert "{struct-series-type-form on ("{series-type}_s", held)}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-new-form, given (the term series-type, the term series-type-new),
            as [static the series-type* the series-type-new(void) { the series-type* s = (the series-type*)cufet_arena_alloc(sizeof(the series-type)); s->data = NULL; s->len = 0; s->cap = 0; s->home = cufet_arena_here(); return s; }].
        Insert "{series-type-new-form on (series-type, "{series-type}_new")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-ensure-form, given (the term series-type-ensure, the term series-type, the c-language axiom held),
            as [static void the series-type-ensure(the series-type* s) { if (s->len >= s->cap) { int nc = s->cap == 0 ? 4 : s->cap * 2; the held* nd = (the held*)cufet_arena_alloc_in(s->home, (size_t)nc * sizeof(the held)); if (s->len > 0) memcpy(nd, s->data, (size_t)s->len * sizeof(the held)); s->data = nd; s->cap = nc; } }].
        Insert "{series-type-ensure-form on ("{series-type}_ensure", series-type, held)}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-append-form, given (the term series-type, the term series-type-append, the c-language axiom held, the term series-type-ensure),
            as [static the series-type* the series-type-append(the series-type* s, the held v) { the series-type-ensure(s); s->data[s->len++] = v; return s; }].
        Insert "{series-type-append-form on (series-type, "{series-type}_append", held, "{series-type}_ensure")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-prepend-form, given (the term series-type-prepend, the term series-type, the c-language axiom held, the term series-type-ensure),
            as [static void the series-type-prepend(the series-type* s, the held v) { the series-type-ensure(s); if (s->len > 0) memmove(s->data + 1, s->data, (size_t)s->len * sizeof(the held)); s->data[0] = v; s->len++; }].
        Insert "{series-type-prepend-form on ("{series-type}_prepend", series-type, held, "{series-type}_ensure")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-insert-after-form, given (the term series-type-insert-after, the term series-type, the c-language axiom held, the term series-type-ensure),
            as [static void the series-type-insert-after(the series-type* s, int after, the held v) { the series-type-ensure(s); if (s->len > after) memmove(s->data + after + 1, s->data + after, (size_t)(s->len - after) * sizeof(the held)); s->data[after] = v; s->len++; }].
        Insert "{series-type-insert-after-form on ("{series-type}_insert_after", series-type, held, "{series-type}_ensure")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-remove-at-form, given (the term series-type-remove-at, the term series-type, the c-language axiom held),
            as [static void the series-type-remove-at(the series-type* s, int index) { if (s->len - index - 1 > 0) memmove(s->data + index, s->data + index + 1, (size_t)(s->len - index - 1) * sizeof(the held)); s->len--; }].
        Insert "{series-type-remove-at-form on ("{series-type}_remove_at", series-type, held)}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-remove-value-form, given (the term series-type-remove-value, the term series-type, the c-language axiom held, the c-language axiom equal, the term series-type-remove-at),
            as [static void the series-type-remove-value(the series-type* s, the held v) { for (int i = 0; i < s->len; i++) if (the equal) { the series-type-remove-at(s, i); return; } }].
        Insert "{series-type-remove-value-form on ("{series-type}_remove_value", series-type, held, equal, "{series-type}_remove_at")}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-eq-form, given (the term series-type-eq, the term series-type, the c-language axiom c-equal),
            as [static int the series-type-eq(the series-type* a, the series-type* b) { if (a->len != b->len) return 0; for (int i = 0; i < a->len; i++) if (!the c-equal) return 0; return 1; }].
        Insert "{series-type-eq-form on ("{series-type}_eq", series-type, cast c-equal on (element, [a->data[i]], [b->data[i]]))}\n" into out.
        Define c-language series-type-write-form, given (the term series-type-write, the term series-type, the c-language axiom written),
            as [static void the series-type-write(the series-type* s) { fputs("(", stdout); for (int i = 0; i < s->len; i++) { if (i > 0) fputs(", ", stdout); the written; } fputs(")", stdout); }].
        Insert "{series-type-write-form on ("{series-type}_write", series-type, written)}\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// Every series type a program may use, and the range that makes a series of numbers.
    Bind text to c-series-prelude:
        Define out as a chase.
        For each element in a series of text with ("number", "text", "fact", "bits"), repeat:
            Insert cast c-series-helpers on (element) into out.
        Done.
        Insert "static cser_number* cser_number_range(CufetDec from, CufetDec to, CufetDec step, int line) {cast c-open}\n" into out.
        Insert "    if (cufet_cmp(step, cufet_dec_from_ll(0)) <= 0) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf(\"the step in 'counting by' must be positive (line %d).\", line));\n" into out.
        Insert "    cser_number* s = cser_number_new();\n" into out.
        Insert "    for (CufetDec n = from; cufet_cmp(n, to) <= 0; n = cufet_add(n, step)) cser_number_append(s, n);\n" into out.
        Insert "    return s;\n{cast c-close}\n\n" into out.
        Return out converted to text.
    Done.

    /// A series, already as C, as the text `State` prints for it: each element's text, measured,
    /// then copied into one arena string. A series of series nests by depth, which keeps the inner
    /// names from shadowing the outer ones they read.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-series-text, given (the text kind, the c-language axiom value, the number depth):
        Define element as cast element-of on (kind).
        Define c-language item-held, given (the term held-series, the term index), as [(the held-series)->data[the index]].
        Define at as item-held on ("cf_ts{depth}", "cf_ti{depth}").
        Define piece as cast no-c.
        If cast element-of on (element) is not "":
            The piece becomes cast c-series-text on (element, at, depth + 1) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise if element is "number" or element is "fact" or element is "text" or element is "bits":
            The piece becomes cast c-text-from on (element, at) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Otherwise:
            Return a failure (cast not-built on ("a series of {element} as text")).
        Done.
        Define c-language series-shown, given (the term series-c, the term held, the c-language axiom value, the term count,
                the term pieces, the term size, the term index, the c-language axiom piece, the term out, the term cursor, the term length),
            as [({ the series-c* the held = the value; int the count = (the held)->len;
char** the pieces = (char**)cufet_arena_alloc((size_t)(the count > 0 ? the count : 1) * sizeof(char*)); size_t the size = 2;
for (int the index = 0; the index < the count; the index++) { the pieces[the index] = the piece; the size += strlen(the pieces[the index]) + (the index > 0 ? 2 : 0); }
char* the out = (char*)cufet_arena_alloc(the size + 1); char* the cursor = the out; *the cursor++ = '(';
for (int the index = 0; the index < the count; the index++) { if (the index > 0) { *the cursor++ = ','; *the cursor++ = ' '; }
size_t the length = strlen(the pieces[the index]); memcpy(the cursor, the pieces[the index], the length); the cursor += the length; }
*the cursor++ = ')'; *the cursor = 0; the out; })].
        Return series-shown on (cast series-c-name on (element), "cf_ts{depth}", value, "cf_tn{depth}", "cf_tp{depth}", "cf_tl{depth}",
            "cf_ti{depth}", piece, "cf_to{depth}", "cf_tw{depth}", "cf_tk{depth}").
    Done.

    /// What a refusal calls the series it reaches into: its name, when it has one.
    Bind text to series-label, given (the node target):
        If target's kind is "VariableReference", return cast unquoted on (cast field-of on (target, 1)).
        Return "series".
    Done.

    // ── Expressions ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The kind a series expression gives, or a failure when it is beyond this compiler.
    Bind text or failure to series-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral":
            Define element as "void".
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) is false:
                The element becomes cast one's kind-of-type on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            // `a series with (10, 20)` names no type — its items do.
            Otherwise if the number of (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children is greater than 0:
                The element becomes cast one's kind-of on (item 1 of (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            If cast is-element-kind on (element) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("a series of {element}")).
            If cast element-of on (element) is not "" or cast is-voidable on (element), cast one's register-series on (element).
            Return "series of {element}".
        Done.
        If kind is "RangeExpression", return "series of number".
        If kind is "SeriesLength", return "number".
        // `item … of`, `the first of`, `the last of`.
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-record on (held), return cast one's record-item-kind on (held, cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        If held is "chase", return "text".
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        If element is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("an item of a {held}")).
        Return element.
    Done.

    /// A series expression as C.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-series-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define kind as expression's kind.
        If kind is "SeriesLiteral":
            Define element as cast element-of on (cast one's series-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off).
            Define series-c as cast series-c-name on (element).
            If the number of (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children is 0, return call-of-one on ("{series-c}_new", cast no-c).
            // One statement per item, so the items are worked out in the order they are written —
            // C leaves the order of a call's arguments open, and gcc takes them last first.
            Define c-language item-added, given (the c-language axiom added, the term adder, the c-language axiom element),
                as [the added cf_sl = the adder(cf_sl, the element);].
            Define built as cast no-c.
            For each written in (cast field-of on (expression, 1))'s children, repeat:
                The built becomes item-added on (built, "{series-c}_append", cast one's c-of-as on (written, element) or pass the failure off).
            Done.
            Define c-language series-made, given (the term series-c, the term maker, the c-language axiom built),
                as [({ the series-c* cf_sl = the maker(); the built cf_sl; })].
            Return series-made on (series-c, "{series-c}_new", built).
        Done.
        If kind is "RangeExpression":
            Define lowest as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
            Define upto as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Define step as call-of-one on ("cufet_dec_from_ll", [1]).
            If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) is false:
                The step becomes cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)) or pass the failure off.
            Done.
            Define c-language range-made, given (the c-language axiom lowest, the c-language axiom upto, the c-language axiom step, the number at-line),
                as [cser_number_range(the lowest, the upto, the step, the at-line)].
            Return range-made on (lowest, upto, step, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 4))).
        Done.
        Define target as cast field-of on (expression, 1).
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If kind is "SeriesAccess" and cast is-record on (target-kind):
            Return cast one's c-record-item on (series-c, target-kind, cast field-of on (expression, 2)) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define at-line as cast line-number on (cast field-of on (expression, 3)).
        If kind is "SeriesAccess" and target-kind is "chase":
            Return cast one's c-chase-item on (target, cast field-of on (expression, 2), at-line) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define element as cast element-of on (target-kind).
        If kind is "SeriesLength":
            Define c-language length-held, given (the c-language axiom held-series), as [cufet_dec_from_ll((the held-series)->len)].
            Return length-held on (series-c).
        Done.
        // `item … of`: the series is held once, so it is reached once.
        Define place as cast one's c-place on (cast field-of on (expression, 2), [cf_at], target, at-line) or pass the failure off.
        Define c-language item-reached, given (the term series-type, the c-language axiom held-series, the c-language axiom place),
            as [({ the series-type* cf_at = the held-series; cf_at->data[the place]; })].
        Return item-reached on (cast series-c-name on (element), series-c, place).
    Done.

    /// The zero-based place of an item in the series `held` names in C — `_` for the last — checked
    /// against its length, as the language refuses an item that is not there.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-place unto emitter, given (the node index, the c-language axiom held, the node target, the number at-line):
        If cast is-nothing on (index), return cast c-place-at on (cast no-c, held, target, at-line).
        Return cast c-place-at on (cast one's c-of on (index) or pass the failure off, held, target, at-line).
    Done.

    /// `c-place` with the index already as C — "" for the last.
    Bind c-language axiom to c-place-at, given (the c-language axiom index-c, the c-language axiom held, the node target, the number at-line):
        Define label as cast series-label on (target).
        If cast is-no-c on (index-c):
            Define c-language last-place, given (the c-language axiom held, the text label, the number at-line),
                as [cufet_last_check((the held)->len, the label, the at-line) - 1].
            Return last-place on (held, label, at-line).
        Done.
        Define c-language checked-place, given (the c-language axiom index, the c-language axiom held, the text label, the number at-line),
            as [cufet_idx_check(cufet_to_int(the index), (the held)->len, the label, the at-line) - 1].
        Return checked-place on (index-c, held, label, at-line).
    Done.

    /// `<series> sorted`, `in reverse`, `by the <field>` — a new series, the old one left as it was.
    Bind text or failure to sorted-kind-of unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If held is "chase", return "chase".
        If cast element-of on (held) is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("sorting a {held}")).
        Return held.
    Done.

    /// The function a sort is `by`, or nothing: a function written in place, or one named — which
    /// the tree also leaves in the field's place, beside a `:KeyFunction` saying what it is.
    Bind node to sort-key-function, given (the node expression):
        If cast is-nothing on (cast field-of on (expression, 6)) is false, return cast field-of on (expression, 6).
        Define place as 0.
        For each part in expression's children, repeat:
            Increment place by 1.
            If part's word is ":KeyFunction", return item (place + 1) of expression's children.
        Done.
        Return cast field-of on (expression, 6).
    Done.

    /// The key a sort compares: the element, or its field.
    Bind text or failure to sort-key-kind unto emitter, given (the text element, the node by-field):
        If cast is-nothing on (by-field), return element.
        Define field-name as cast unquoted on (by-field).
        If cast is-record on (element), return cast record-field-kind on (element, field-name).
        If cast object-of on (element) is not "", return cast one's field-kind on (cast object-of on (element), field-name) or pass the failure off.
        Return "".
    Done.

    /// Whether one key is past the next: the test a sort moves on.
    Bind c-language axiom to out-of-order, given (the c-language axiom compared, the fact reversed):
        Define c-language past-next, given (the c-language axiom compared), as [(the compared) > 0].
        Define c-language before-last, given (the c-language axiom compared), as [(the compared) < 0].
        If reversed, return before-last on (compared).
        Return past-next on (compared).
    Done.

    /// A sort as C: a copy, put in order by a stable insertion sort — equal keys keep their order, as
    /// the interpreter's does. Numbers compare as numbers; text by its bytes, as `cufet build` has it.
    /// `<series> in reverse` — a new series, the items appended last to first.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-reversed unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        If cast element-of on (held) is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("reversing a {held}")).
        Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (cast element-of on (held)).
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define c-language reversed-copy, given (the term series-type, the c-language axiom held-series, the term maker, the term adder),
            as [({ the series-type* cf_src = the held-series; the series-type* cf_dst = the maker(); for (int cf_i = cf_src->len - 1; cf_i >= 0; cf_i--) the adder(cf_dst, cf_src->data[cf_i]); cf_dst; })].
        Return reversed-copy on (series-type, series-c, "{series-type}_new", "{series-type}_append").
    Done.

    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-sorted unto emitter, given (the node expression):
        Define held as cast one's sorted-kind-of on (expression) or pass the failure off.
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (cast field-of on (expression, 1)) or pass the failure off.
        Define reversed as (cast field-of on (expression, 3))'s word is "true".
        If held is "chase":
            Define c-language chase-sorted, given (the c-language axiom held-series, the fact reversed), as [cufet_chase_sorted(the held-series, the reversed)].
            Return chase-sorted on (series-c, reversed).
        Done.
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (element).
        Define key-function as cast sort-key-function on (expression).
        If cast is-nothing on (key-function) is false:
            Return cast one's c-sorted-by-function on (series-c, element, key-function, reversed) or pass the failure off.
        Done.
        Define by-field as cast field-of on (expression, 2).
        Define key-kind as cast one's sort-key-kind on (element, by-field) or pass the failure off.
        Define left-key as bracketed on ([cf_dst->data[cf_j]]).
        Define right-key as bracketed on ([cf_k]).
        If cast is-nothing on (by-field) is false:
            Define member as cast c-name on (cast unquoted on (by-field)).
            The left-key becomes field-read on ([cf_dst->data[cf_j]], member).
            The right-key becomes field-read on ([cf_k], member).
        Done.
        Define compared as cast no-c.
        If key-kind is "number", the compared becomes call-of-two on ("cufet_cmp", left-key, right-key).
        Otherwise if key-kind is "text", the compared becomes call-of-two on ("strcmp", left-key, right-key).
        Otherwise, return a failure (cast not-built on ("sorting by a {key-kind}")).
        Define c-language sorted-copy, given (the term series-type, the c-language axiom held-series, the term maker, the term adder,
                the c-language axiom element-c, the c-language axiom out-of-order),
            as [({ the series-type* cf_src = the held-series; the series-type* cf_dst = the maker(); for (int cf_i = 0; cf_i < cf_src->len; cf_i++) the adder(cf_dst, cf_src->data[cf_i]); for (int cf_a = 1; cf_a < cf_dst->len; cf_a++) { the element-c cf_k = cf_dst->data[cf_a]; int cf_j = cf_a - 1; while (cf_j >= 0 && the out-of-order) { cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_dst->data[cf_j]; cf_j--; } cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_k; } cf_dst; })].
        Return sorted-copy on (series-type, series-c, "{series-type}_new", "{series-type}_append", cast c-type on (element),
            cast out-of-order on (compared, reversed)).
    Done.

    /// `<series> sorted by <function>` — the same stable sort, over keys worked out UP FRONT, each
    /// once and in order, as the interpreter does; they move with their items.
    Bind c-language axiom or failure to c-sorted-by-function unto emitter, given (the c-language axiom series-c, the text element,
            the node key-function, the fact reversed):
        Define function-kind as cast one's kind-of on (key-function) or pass the failure off.
        Define key-kind as cast function-gives on (function-kind).
        If key-kind is not "number" and key-kind is not "text", return a failure (cast not-built on ("sorting by a function giving a {key-kind}")).
        Define function-c as cast one's c-of on (key-function) or pass the failure off.
        Define compared as call-of-two on ("strcmp", [cf_keys->data[cf_j]], [cf_kk]).
        If key-kind is "number", the compared becomes call-of-two on ("cufet_cmp", [cf_keys->data[cf_j]], [cf_kk]).
        Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (element).
        Define keys-type as cast series-c-name on (key-kind).
        Define c-language sorted-by-keys, given (the term series-type, the c-language axiom held-series, the term maker, the term keys-type, the term keys-maker,
                the term function-type, the c-language axiom function-c, the term adder, the term keys-append, the c-language axiom element-c,
                the c-language axiom key-c, the c-language axiom out-of-order),
            as [({ the series-type* cf_src = the held-series; the series-type* cf_dst = the maker(); the keys-type* cf_keys = the keys-maker(); the function-type cf_kf = the function-c; for (int cf_i = 0; cf_i < cf_src->len; cf_i++) { the adder(cf_dst, cf_src->data[cf_i]); the keys-append(cf_keys, cf_kf.fn(cf_kf.env, cf_src->data[cf_i])); } for (int cf_a = 1; cf_a < cf_dst->len; cf_a++) { the element-c cf_k = cf_dst->data[cf_a]; the key-c cf_kk = cf_keys->data[cf_a]; int cf_j = cf_a - 1; while (cf_j >= 0 && the out-of-order) { cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_dst->data[cf_j]; cf_keys->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_keys->data[cf_j]; cf_j--; } cf_dst->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_k; cf_keys->data[cf_j + 1] = cf_kk; } cf_dst; })].
        Return sorted-by-keys on (series-type, series-c, "{series-type}_new", keys-type, "{keys-type}_new", cast function-c-name on (function-kind), function-c,
            "{series-type}_append", "{keys-type}_append", cast c-type on (element), cast c-type on (key-kind), cast out-of-order on (compared, reversed)).
    Done.

    // ── Statements ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

    /// The kind of a series' elements, for a statement that changes it.
    Bind text or failure to changed-element unto emitter, given (the node target):
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        If element is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("changing a {held}")).
        Return element.
    Done.

    Bind void or failure to emit-series-statement unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define kind as statement's kind.
        If kind is "ForEachStatement":
            Cast one's emit-for-each on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesInsertStatement":
            Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
            If (cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off) is "chase":
                Cast one's emit-chase-insert on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define insert-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-set on (insert-kind):
                Cast one's emit-set-insert on (statement, insert-kind) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 1), element) or pass the failure off.
            // The series, then the value, then the place, as the interpreter works them out.
            Define operands as a series of node with (target, cast field-of on (statement, 1)).
            Define sides as a series of c-language axiom with (series-c, value).
            Define following as cast field-of on (statement, 3).
            If cast is-nothing on (following) is false:
                Insert following into operands.
                Define following-c as cast one's c-of on (following) or pass the failure off.
                Insert following-c into sides.
            Done.
            Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, sides).
            Define series-type as cast series-c-name on (element).
            If (cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word is "true":
                Cast one's put on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, done-with on (call-of-two on ("{series-type}_prepend", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides)))).
                Return.
            Done.
            If cast is-nothing on (following):
                Cast one's put on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, done-with on (call-of-two on ("{series-type}_append", item 1 of sides, item 2 of sides)))).
                Return.
            Done.
            Cast one's put on (cast in-order-statement on (prefix, done-with on (call-of-three on ("{series-type}_insert_after", item 1 of sides, call-of-one on ("cufet_to_int", item 3 of sides), item 2 of sides)))).
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesRemoveValueStatement":
            Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
            // `Remove <key> from <map>` is written the same way.
            Define target-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            If cast is-map on (target-kind):
                Cast one's emit-map-remove on (statement, target-kind) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            If target-kind is "chase":
                Cast one's emit-chase-remove on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define sides as cast one's c-fields-in-order on (statement, 1, 2) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's put on (cast in-order-statement on (item 1 of sides, done-with on (call-of-two on ("{cast series-c-name on (element)}_remove_value", item 2 of sides, item 3 of sides)))).
            Return.
        Done.
        If kind is "SeriesRemoveAtStatement":
            Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
            If (cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off) is "chase":
                Cast one's emit-chase-remove on (statement) or pass the failure off.
                Return.
            Done.
            Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define place as cast one's c-place on (cast field-of on (statement, 2), [cf_at], target,
                cast line-number on (cast field-of on (statement, 3))) or pass the failure off.
            Define c-language series-c-name-remove-at-form, given (the term series-c-name, the c-language axiom series-c, the term series-c-name-remove-at, the c-language axiom place),
                as [{ the series-c-name* cf_at = the series-c; the series-c-name-remove-at(cf_at, the place); }].
            Cast one's put on (series-c-name-remove-at-form on (cast series-c-name on (element), series-c, "{cast series-c-name on (element)}_remove_at", place)).
            Return.
        Done.
        // `The item … of … becomes …`.
        Define target as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define set-kind as cast one's kind-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        If set-kind is "chase":
            Cast one's emit-chase-set on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-record on (set-kind):
            If cast is-place on (target) is false, return a failure (cast not-built on ("setting a field of something that is not a name")).
            Define record-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
            Define member as cast one's c-record-item on (record-c, set-kind, cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Define part-held as cast one's record-item-kind on (set-kind, cast field-of on (statement, 2)) or pass the failure off.
            Cast one's put on (assigned-to on (member, cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), part-held) or pass the failure off)).
            Return.
        Done.
        Define element as cast one's changed-element on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (target) or pass the failure off.
        Define value as cast one's c-of-as on (cast field-of on (statement, 3), element) or pass the failure off.
        // The series, then the place, then the value — C leaves an assignment's two sides unordered.
        Define index as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define operands as a series of node with (target, cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
        Define sides as a series of c-language axiom with (series-c, value).
        If cast is-nothing on (index) is false:
            Define index-c as cast one's c-of on (index) or pass the failure off.
            The operands becomes a series of node with (target, index, cast field-of on (statement, 3)).
            The sides becomes a series of c-language axiom with (series-c, index-c, value).
        Done.
        Define prefix as cast order-prefix on (operands, sides).
        Define place as cast c-place-at on (cast no-c, [cf_at], target, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (statement, 4))).
        If cast is-nothing on (index) is false:
            The place becomes cast c-place-at on (item 2 of sides, [cf_at], target, cast line-number on (cast field-of on (statement, 4))).
        Done.
        Define c-language item-set, given (the c-language axiom prefix, the term series-type, the c-language axiom held-series, the c-language axiom place, the c-language axiom value),
            as [{ the prefix the series-type* cf_at = the held-series; cf_at->data[the place] = the value; }].
        Cast one's put on (item-set on (prefix, cast series-c-name on (element), item 1 of sides, place, item (the number of sides) of sides)).
    Done.

    /// `For each <name> in <series>, repeat:` — over the items there when it began, as in C#. The
    /// name, or `it`, holds each in turn and is gone when the loop ends.
    Bind void or failure to emit-for-each unto emitter, given (the node statement):
        Define named as cast field-of on (statement, 1).
        Define name as "it".
        If cast is-nothing on (named) is false, the name becomes cast unquoted on (named).
        Define over as cast field-of on (statement, 2).
        Define held as cast one's kind-of on (over) or pass the failure off.
        If cast is-map on (held):
            Cast one's emit-map-for-each on (statement, held) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If cast is-set on (held):
            Cast one's emit-set-for-each on (statement, held) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        If held is "chase":
            Cast one's emit-chase-for-each on (statement) or pass the failure off.
            Return.
        Done.
        Define element as cast element-of on (held).
        If element is "", return a failure (cast not-built on ("looping over a {held}")).
        Define series-c as cast one's c-of on (over) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's put on ([{]).
        Define kept as a map from text to text.
        For each pair in one's kinds, repeat:
            In kept, the entry for the key of pair becomes the value of pair.
        Done.
        Define outer as one's indent.
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define c-language series-name-each-form, given (the term series-c-name, the c-language axiom series-c),
            as [the series-c-name* cf_each = the series-c;].
        Cast one's put on (series-name-each-form on (cast series-c-name on (element), series-c)).
        Cast one's put on ([int cf_each_n = cf_each->len;]).
        // ⚠ Inserting into or removing from the series it loops over is refused while it runs —
        // checked before each pass and once more on the way out, which `Stop` leaves without, as
        // the interpreter does (GRAMMAR: "The for-each body cannot add or remove elements").
        Cast one's put on ([for (int cf_i = 0; ; cf_i++) {]).
        In one's kinds, the entry for name becomes element.
        Cast one's declared-here on (name).
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "        ".
        Define c-language each-len-each-form, given (the text message),
            as [if (cf_each->len != cf_each_n) cufet_raise(cufet_msgf(the message));].
        Cast one's put on (each-len-each-form on ("'{cast series-label on (over)}' was modified during a for-each loop on line {(cast field-of on (statement, 4))'s word} — collect into a separate series, or use a While loop if you need to change it while looping.")).
        Cast one's put on ([if (cf_i >= cf_each_n) break;]).
        Define c-language type-name-each-form, given (the c-language axiom c-type, the term c-name),
            as [the c-type the c-name = cf_each->data[cf_i];].
        Cast one's put on (type-name-each-form on (cast c-type on (element), cast c-name on (name))).
        The one's indent becomes outer joined to "    ".
        Define loop-kept as cast one's entering-loop.
        Cast one's emit-block on (cast field-of on (statement, 3)) or pass the failure off.
        Cast one's leaving-loop on (loop-kept).
        Cast one's put on ([}]).
        The one's indent becomes outer.
        The one's kinds becomes kept.
        Cast one's put on ([}]).
    Done.
Done.
